AssertionError: expected undefined to be true // Object.is equality — src/app/admin/actions.test.ts:789:23
TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading '0') — src/app/admin/actions.test.ts:837:39, :858:39
- resolved: the suite's fake claim row was `bookingRow({ status: "cancelled" })` with `cancelledAt: null`, which the real claim never returns; the new `claimedAt()` guard refused it (→ `refund-failed`, no Stripe call). The claim fixtures now carry a `cancelledAt` (`claimedRow()`), as the real UPDATE … RETURNING does.
- rule: a test that fakes `cancelAndRefundBooking`'s claim must return a row with `cancelledAt` set — the tour refund's idempotency key is read from it (`web/src/lib/booking-refund.ts` → `claimedAt`).
