## 2026-10-01T13:19:57Z ci Quality (advisory) — src/lib/quote-refund.test.ts (2 failed) after b22a46c
AssertionError: expected { …(21) } to match object { status: 'refunded', … } — src/lib/quote-refund.test.ts:400:38 (received refundedAmountCents 28800, status "paid")
AssertionError: expected "vi.fn()" to be called 2 times, but got 1 times — src/lib/quote-refund.test.ts:981:29
- resolved: the replay guard (`refund.id === payment.stripeRefundId`) is right for Stripe, whose refund ids are unique, but `stripeRefundsAsAsked()` minted `re_admin_<amount>` for every refund, so a second deliberate refund of the same amount looked like a replay of the first. The stand-in now gives each refund its own id (`re_admin_<amount>_<n>` from the second on).
- rule: a Stripe stand-in in `web/src/lib/quote-refund.test.ts` must give every created refund a distinct id — the admin path treats a refund id the row already holds as a replay.
